-- title:
--   Unramifiedness at the auxiliary prime of the Taylor–Wiles Hecke representation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field, and let $p$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, that is, a two-dimensional $k$-space with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to its endomorphisms which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $N$ a nonzero natural all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, and $r$ a prime with $r\nmid N$, $r\neq p$, $p\nmid r-1$, such that $\bar\rho$ is unramified at $r$ (inertia at every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $r$ among its nonunits acts trivially) and such that for every such valuation subring $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra with $S$ omitted, namely the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct nonzero primes outside $S$, each different from $r$, let $\pi_{\Delta,i}\colon(\mathbb{Z}/q_i)^\times\to\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/p^{v_p(q_i-1)})$ be homomorphisms, and let $\alpha\colon\mathrm{Fin}\,t\to k$. With $H_Q=\mathtt{HQ}$ the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/(N\prod_i q_i\cdot r))^\times$ cut out by $\mathtt{HR}$ and the kernel of $\pi_Q$, assume the commutation hypotheses `OpComm` (the Hecke operators attached to the generators commute with one another) and `DiaComm` (the diamond operators commute with them). Let $\mathbb{T}=\mathtt{HeckeRing}$ be the resulting $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the Hecke generators acting on the localised cohomology module, and assume: $\mathbb{T}$ is local, Noetherian, adically complete for its maximal ideal, finite as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, the structure map $\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{T}$ is a local homomorphism, and its composite with the residue map of $\mathbb{T}$ is surjective. Finally let $\rho'$ be a Galois representation over $\mathbb{T}$ (a free finite $\mathbb{T}$-module of rank $2$ with an adically continuous action) whose traces of Frobenius at every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N\prod_i q_i\cdot r$ equal the corresponding Hecke operator $T_\ell$ in $\mathbb{T}$, and whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Then $\rho'$ is unramified at $r$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $r$ among its nonunits, $\rho'$ is trivial on the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the Galois representation carried by the Taylor–Wiles-level Hecke ring is unramified at the auxiliary prime $r$, which enters the argument only to make the relevant congruence subgroup torsion-free; the numerical conditions $p\nmid r-1$ and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\neq(r+1)^2$ rule out ramification at $r$. It is used in the construction of the modular deformation over the Hecke ring at Taylor–Wiles level, where the deformation must be of the prescribed type unramified outside $S$ and the set of Taylor–Wiles primes.
